WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.443
$7,000 of tax-free savings account, or TFSA, room in January removes December deadline risk. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 200. Episode 200. Thanks for sticking with us. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:30.443 --> 00:00:35.343
American indexes finished lower today while energy stocks lifted the Toronto Stock

00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:47.676
Exchange Composite, or TSX, to 35,983.98. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,805.45. The NASDAQ

00:00:47.676 --> 00:00:57.336
Composite closed at 27,204, up 17.08% year to date, and up 21.59% since this show's practice

00:00:57.336 --> 00:01:02.816
record began. The nearest bank of Canada and Federal Reserve decisions remain the key macro

00:01:02.816 --> 00:01:09.656
frame around that split tape. About 15 days ago we simulated IAG on a segregated fund milestone,

00:01:10.176 --> 00:01:16.236
and the 1.73 percent decline on the clothes underscored that inflows alone do not guarantee short-term

00:01:16.236 --> 00:01:22.594
outperformance when sector rotation is active. Motley Fool Canada walks through a planning tactic

00:01:22.594 --> 00:01:28.074
most people still leave until the last weeks of the year. Move the annual TFSA contribution

00:01:28.074 --> 00:01:34.014
as soon as the new room opens, instead of waiting for a December cash scramble. The 2026

00:01:34.014 --> 00:01:38.914
contribution room is the figure that article uses, and the mechanic is a simple transfer

00:01:38.914 --> 00:01:44.934
from a non-registered account or a cash balance on any brokerage platform. January 1st is when

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:49.734
that new room becomes available, so the transfer can sit in the account before year-end bills

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:52.214
and bonuses start competing for the same dollars.

00:01:52.774 --> 00:01:57.474
The approach has worked best in years when contribution room changes or tax your deadlines

00:01:57.474 --> 00:02:01.494
create last minute rushes, which is exactly when people miss the window.

00:02:02.134 --> 00:02:07.854
The main risk is opportunity cost if that cash earns higher interest outside the TFSA, but

00:02:07.854 --> 00:02:11.294
that drag is usually small relative to the planning certainty you gain.

00:02:11.854 --> 00:02:14.994
You are not chasing a bigger immediate tax saving with this move.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:19.714
You are removing deadline risk and the chance that December cash flow pressure leaves the

00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:25.094
room unfilled. Implementation is the boring part on purpose. Open the TFSA

00:02:25.094 --> 00:02:29.454
contribution ticket, pull the cash across and leave the investing decisions for

00:02:29.454 --> 00:02:33.334
after the room is locked. Open your brokerage statement, find the

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:37.574
contribution room line, and set a calendar reminder for the first business day of

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:42.854
2027 to move the full annual amount in immediately. That reminder is the

00:02:42.854 --> 00:02:48.978
whole tactic. The contribution is the plan. December

00:02:48.978 --> 00:02:55.138
After mining, ticker EDV on the TSX is today's simulated weekly hold, and this is a simulated

00:02:55.138 --> 00:02:58.058
trade for learning purposes with no real money involved.

